# promise: #855
# Help ▸ Troubleshooting ▸ Open Task Manager opens Chrome's own Task Manager, as Arc's does, also with no tab in
# front: the page opened in the background is enough. Before, Cra asked only the page in front and said "Open a
# Page First" while other pages were open.
budget rss=900 stalls50=20
ends-a-page
seed settings.json {"hasSeenImportPrompt": true, "toolbarDefaultMigrated": true}
pace 0.5

cra://open?url=${PAGE}?n=background&background=1
expect-log GET /page\.html\?n=background
wait 2
cra://action/taskManager
expect-log task manager: opened from another open page
wait 3
cra://debug?chromeWindows=tm
expect-log chrome window tm: .*'Task [Mm]anager'
reject-log task manager: no page open

# Its End task ends the page's process, as for a frozen tab: the page goes and Cra stays (the harness checks it runs).
cra://debug?taskManagerEnd=Fixture
expect-log task manager end Fixture: pressed for Tab: Fixture
expect-log page process ended \((killed|abnormal termination)\)
